Lua 5.1.5 (https://www.lua.org) and LuaJIT 2.1 (https://luajit.org)

lua/parse is a port of their lexers and parsers: the
lexer (lexer.go) of Lua 5.1's llex.c and LuaJIT's lj_lex.c, the parser
(parser.go) of Lua 5.1's lparser.c and LuaJIT's lj_parse.c, the model of
Lua 5.1's register allocation (lua51regs.go) of lcode.c, and the model of
LuaJIT's code generator (jitcode.go, by way of go-luascope below) of
lj_parse.c and lj_bc.h. Both are under the MIT License, whose text is the
one above, with these copyright lines:

Copyright (C) 1994-2012 Lua.org, PUC-Rio.

Copyright (C) 2005-2017 Mike Pall. All rights reserved.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
go-luascope (https://github.com/bigbes/go-luascope, now luascope/)

lua/parse/strscan.go, the number scanner of the LuaJIT dialect, is
adapted from go-luascope's parser/number.go, a port of LuaJIT's
lj_strscan.c (LuaJIT, Copyright (C) 2005-2017 Mike Pall, MIT License; the
MIT License text is the one above, with that copyright line).

lua/parse/jitcode.go, the model of LuaJIT's code generator the parser runs
in the LuaJIT dialect, and its calls in lua/parse/parser.go are adapted
from go-luascope's parser/codegen.go, parser/bytecode.go, parser/scope.go
and parser/parser_stmt.go, ports of LuaJIT's lj_parse.c and lj_bc.h (same
copyright and license as lj_strscan.c above); lua/parse/jitcode_test.go
has go-luascope's limit and code generator snippets
(parser/snippets_test.go) and their results.

